Note to self =E2=80=94 for a future philset design session.

## The pattern
Company repos (all of plastic-labs, and probably beyond) ship their own
CLAUDE.md that already documents architecture. Maintaining a separate
.meta/logical-architecture.md alongside it is redundant and drifts. So:
in projects configured for it, treat CLAUDE.md AS the architecture doc =E2=
=80=94
/hello should NOT offer to generate logical-architecture.md, and when
architecture changes during a session, the update target is CLAUDE.md.

## Proposed signpost flag
- `architecture-doc: CLAUDE.md` (path, relative to project root) =E2=80=94 =
names
the file that IS the architecture doc. When set:
* /hello skips the logical-architecture.md generate/maintenance offer
* architecture-change tracking points here instead
* default (unset) preserves today's behavior (.meta/logical-architecture.md=
)
- Consider whether the existing boolean `architecture:` flag should be
folded into this (e.g. `architecture: false` | `true` | `<path>`), or
kept separate. Separate is cleaner to reason about; overloading is fewer
flags. Design call.

Inherited down the tree (set once at a domain level, applies to all
projects under it) =E2=80=94 hunch is one line at plastic-labs covers every=
 repo.

## Stopgap already on this machine (so the library update won't surprise us=
)
In ~/Development/plastic-labs/.meta/signpost.yml I added:
architecture: false # understood today; suppresses the logical-arch offer
architecture-doc: CLAUDE.md # additive/forward-compat; inert until philset
formalizes it
`architecture-doc` is an unknown flag to the current library, so it's
inert (ignored) =E2=80=94 nothing breaks. `architecture: false` is already
understood and does the suppression today. When the library learns
`architecture-doc`, this config should Just Work without edits.

## Design-session checklist
- [ ] Canonical flag shape: separate `architecture-doc` vs. overloaded
`architecture`
- [ ] /hello step 4 changes (skip offer, maybe surface "arch doc:
CLAUDE.md" in summary)
- [ ] Where does /review's architecture dimension read from when this is
set?
- [ ] Does "track architecture changes" mean /hello nudges when code
structure
drifts from CLAUDE.md? (parallels the current logical-architecture.md
staleness check in step 4)
- [ ] Backward-compat: unset flag =3D=3D current behavior; verify no machin=
e
breaks

Captured 2026-07-22 during a groudon session.

